<!--CLI Documentation — Configuration
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.Configuration-->
<clidoc:Configuration xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidoc="com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    MachineBlocks defaults and blockml.config.json fields this host reads
  </is>
  <documentation>
    The host reads blockml.config.json from the project root, the same file
    @blockml/cli reads. It understands the universal keys and these MachineBlocks
    keys. The universal CLI documents the MachineBlocks keys as unread in its V1;
    this host is the reader.

    Universal keys this host honours:

    - srcDir — default blocks. Project BML sources, and the only compile output
      root. Target FQNs are resolved to paths inside this directory. Compile
      does not read outDir and does not accept --out.
    - libraries — extra Library.bml seeds, appended to package.json blockml.library.
    - targetOptions — opaque bag. Key machineblocks-v3-scad may carry
      settingsFormat (pseudo-map or object). V1 emit is pseudo-map; object is
      rejected with a diagnostic until the SCAD library accepts it.
    - defaultTarget — this host treats machineblocks-v3-scad as the default even
      when the key is omitted. If the key is set to another name, the host
      reports that this command only compiles the SCAD target.

    MachineBlocks keys:

    - mbLibPath — root used to compute relative use/include paths to the SCAD
      library (lib/block.scad, config/mb_config.scad, service .scad files).
      Default: the installed @machineblocks/core package root.
    - openscadPath — OpenSCAD executable for later thumbnail or preview commands.
      Not required for compile.
    - thumbsDir — output directory for later thumbnail generation.
    - activeConfig — named config profile inside the SCAD library. Optional.
    - bmlExtensions — extra filename suffixes treated as BML. Default .bml.

    targets[] on the universal CLI defaults to ["blockdoc"] and must not be
    required for this host. The host registers machineblocks-v3-scad itself.
    Unknown toolchain target names are not an error here; they are ignored
    because this command does not bootstrap them.

    bom-cli.config.json renaming is not part of this package.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidoc:TargetBootstrap" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</clidoc:Configuration>
